ts journey into interstellar space continues.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>What has changed in James Bond films over the decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:254781bca3c1450d87a228f38b9acc59966422be3b92f044cd7e549ea04f4045</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001--7d894a9cd4fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1962, a martini-drinking womanizer saved the world for the first time in "Dr. No." As Robert Pattinson takes on the role of 007, here's how the films evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia scandal: China's chips dilemma, US rivalry shape AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f50df919bc7edb0ac5b8ea8fcef204bd74788cc7a201b383d1d99340c0b9c2f3</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-scandal-china-s-chips-dilemma-us-rivalry-shape-ai-race/a-79961766--39b6798086ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-scandal-china-s-chips-dilemma-us-rivalry-shape-ai-race/a-79961766?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The controversy surrounding Nvidia and its former CEO Jensen Huang has put a spotlight on the intensifying AI race between the US and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla planning €3BN investment in German factory to produce Cybercabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb234afa6a34738afe06f1bc7e0b716473222a83394a444ae9fc5767100fcb1f</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-_3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416--56a989627169.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-€3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Elon Musk-owned company is looking to further expand its only European production line. Brandenburg's state leader has welcomed the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: how close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a81cb1bc63161c3180303390e3c2f8897e05284c2dc12a09411f7e2f61d3f1e</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:419a77fff068ff7dd0d9566606068efb854b1613b813a2bb2ffd12d0ff3c6605</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British actor Robert Pattinson confirmed as new James Bond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a72437b46e86a7cd8a0bf67732f674df776b375e282717ea10364b58397d774</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-actor-robert-pattinson-confirmed-as-new-james-bond/a-79961789--55e18f26535e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-actor-robert-pattinson-confirmed-as-new-james-bond/a-79961789?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">James Bond 007 ranks among the longest-running and highest-grossing movie franchises in Hollywood's ​history.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea's gold rush: Arrests, deportations spark outcry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a5ea3261d62b75ff049157d021e5e31e39838e2f0441273cf0bfa2f63102791</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-s-gold-rush-arrests-deportations-spark-outcry/a-79922842--da7e32f94527.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-s-gold-rush-arrests-deportations-spark-outcry/a-79922842?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Guinea has banned illegal gold mining, citing environmental concerns. It has further charged hundreds of suspected local and foreign illegal miners amid reports of rights abuses and deportations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 draft deal calls for 'immediate' shift away from fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84f8143fa6ce5ea6bd26ca02bfdc1a30810a22a778267464a090ed4a613528e3</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705--2a7f1bfc2c85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The preliminary agreement at UN climate talks in Turkey calls for a rapid reduction of planet-warming emissions and at least $120 billion to help countries adapt to climate change.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>China says Xi, Trump, Putin to discuss 'world peace'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e736b918560939dcb49bdeca9507c0aa1ddb97dbe04536c53699ddf6ee1ec723</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-says-xi-trump-putin-to-discuss-world-peace/a-79959570--38e10eb9a3d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-says-xi-trump-putin-to-discuss-world-peace/a-79959570?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China says presidents Xi, Trump and Putin are going to have "in-depth discussions on global peace." Ukraine, Iran and denuclearization could also feature in the talks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, EU states open talks on Rwanda deportation scheme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3967653acd873f51cc7b91d76502cbe278c9f90acddaf059fcdb549d6ae4d012</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-eu-states-open-talks-on-rwanda-deportation-scheme/a-79959158--74e78ce21166.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-eu-states-open-talks-on-rwanda-deportation-scheme/a-79959158?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move follows approval of EU regulations that ease deportations and allow hubs to be set up outside the bloc. A similar scheme by the UK government fell apart over legal issues.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title>